  "metadata": {
    "title": "Cross-referencing Western Australia's vegetation associations to the IUCN Global Ecosystem Typology: 90m Best-Candidate Spatial Synthesis",
    "publication_date": "2026-11-14",
    "description": "<p>This dataset provides a 90 m spatial synthesis and tabular lookup cross-referencing Western Australia's vegetation associations from a statewide vegetation map (<strong>DPIRD 006<\/strong>; 1564 vegetation associations across Western Australia) to Level 3 Ecosystem Functional Groups (EFGs) of the <strong>IUCN Global Ecosystem Typology (IUCN GET)<\/strong>. <\/p>\n\n<p>Cross-referencing relationships were established by 2 domain experts across 3 rounds of structured expert elicitation using fuzzy membership values. This package provides the synthesised <strong>best-candidate ('winner-takes-all')<\/strong> spatial layers from Round 3 (1564 eligible vegetation associations units mapped to 23 IUCN GET Ecosystem Functional Groups, along with pixel-level membership proportions, number of supporting interpreters, tabular cross-reference tables, and GIS styling files.<\/p>\n\n<p><strong>Attribution requirement:<\/strong> Spatial layers are derived from pre-European vegetation mapping of Western Australia (DPIRD-006) from <a href=\"https://catalogue.data.wa.gov.au\">dataWA<\/a> &copy;State of Western Australia, Department of Primary Industries and Regional Development. (CC BY 4.0).<\/p>",
